cff-version: 1.2.0
title: quadrat-ipi-eval
message: >-
  If you report numbers produced with this harness, please cite the dataset as well: the harness
  computes, the dataset is what the numbers are about, and a result is only reproducible when both
  are pinned.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A harness for measuring indirect prompt-injection detectors on the Quadrat-IPI dataset. It scores
  every document, picks one threshold over the whole clean pool at a target false-positive rate,
  and reports recall per cell of the lever x objective grid with confidence intervals, rather than
  a single averaged number. Adding a detector is one class with one method; per-document scores are
  saved, so any other operating point or slice can be re-derived without running anything again.
authors:
  - family-names: Gribov
    given-names: Mikhail
    orcid: null
repository-code: https://github.com/mihail-gribov/quadrat-ipi-eval
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - prompt-injection
  - indirect-prompt-injection
  - llm-security
  - evaluation
  - evaluation-harness
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Quadrat-IPI: an evaluation dataset for indirect prompt-injection detectors, on a fixed lever x objective grid"
    authors:
      - family-names: Gribov
        given-names: Mikhail
    year: 2026
    url: https://huggingface.co/datasets/mihailgribov/quadrat-ipi
    notes: >-
      Pin a released version with revision=, and record the build fingerprint the harness writes
      into every result. Without both, a number cannot be traced to the bytes that produced it.
